{"type":"statement","design":"ENGINE_STATEMENT_POINTS","title":"The strategic imperative for pharmacy automation","lead":"Modernizing inventory and fulfillment workflows is essential to protect margins and elevate patient care.","statement":"Unifying pharmacy data with Vertex AI and Gemini turns reactive stock management into predictive fulfillment.","text":"Healthcare supply chain leaders recognize that legacy planning cannot keep pace with dynamic patient demand. Deploying predictive AI models and intelligent workflow agents directly addresses stockouts, fulfillment delays, and planner bottlenecks.","points":[{"title":"Anticipate out-of-stock risks","text":"Healthcare supply chain executives identify predictive demand planning and real-time stockout anticipation as top high-impact AI priorities."},{"title":"Accelerate prescription fills","text":"Intelligent triage between retail stores and central hubs eliminates manual bottlenecks so patients receive critical medications much faster across all regional care locations."},{"title":"Empower supply chain planners","text":"Generative AI assistants automate routine exception analysis and data gathering, doubling planning velocity across the enterprise and freeing teams for higher-value activities."}],"notes":"Modernizing dispensary and supply chain operations is an urgent strategic imperative. McKinsey research shows that healthcare supply chain leaders view predictive demand planning and real-time out-of-stock risk anticipation as top-impact AI use cases. By combining Vertex AI forecasting with Gemini agents, Walgreens can simultaneously improve product availability, speed up prescription fills, and accelerate inventory planning.

