{"type":"process","design":"P66_STEP_FLOW","title":"Automated FinOps and workload cost management","lead":"Continuous slot autoscaling and storage tiering directly drive the target reduction in platform cost.","items":[{"title":"Partition event tables","text":"Partition high-volume telemetry tables by event date and cluster by member identifier to restrict query scans solely to relevant data blocks.","icon":"database"},{"title":"Tier cold storage","text":"Enforce automated lifecycle rules that transition untouched historical partitions to long-term storage pricing without degrading query availability.","icon":"cloud-layers"},{"title":"Isolate workload slots","text":"Route ingestion pipelines, machine learning training, and ad-hoc marketer queries into dedicated autoscaling slot reservations to prevent compute contention.","icon":"gear-cloud"},{"title":"Monitor query spend","text":"Track slot consumption per query via system metadata views and archive dormant staging tables to maintain strict budget governance.","icon":"gear-dollar"}],"points":["Industry benchmark: up to 54% lower 3-year TCO on BigQuery versus cloud alternatives","Industry benchmark: up to 50% storage cost reduction via automated cold data tiering"],"notes":"Enterprise Strategy Group found that BigQuery delivers up to 54% lower three-year TCO compared to alternative cloud data warehouses, while automated tiering for cold data reduces storage expenditures by up to 50%. Combined with table partitioning and workload slot reservations, these FinOps controls directly support the target 25% reduction in data platform cost.

